DOAS.CONF(5)                File Formats

NAME
    doas.conf - the rules of doas

SYNOPSIS
    /etc/doas.conf

DESCRIPTION
    Each line of /etc/doas.conf holds one rule, and the last rule that
    matches a request decides it. A rule has the form

        permit|deny [options] identity [as target] [cmd command [args ...]]

    where identity is an account name, or a group name preceded by a
    colon. A rule without as applies to every target account. A rule
    with cmd applies only to that command, and with args only when the
    arguments are exactly the ones listed. Text from # to the end of the
    line is a comment.

    The options of a permit rule are nopass, which runs the command
    without asking for a password, nolog, which leaves the command out of
    the log, keepenv, which keeps the environment of the caller, and
    setenv { name name=value -name }, which keeps, sets or removes the
    listed variables. The persist option is accepted and has no effect on
    minios.

    The file must belong to root and must not be writable by others.
    doas -C checks a file without running a command. minios ships rules
    that let the members of the group wheel run any command with their
    own password and let root run commands without one.

        permit :wheel
        permit nopass root

    The file is part of the system image, while the membership of wheel
    is kept in /etc/group with the other account databases on the data
    volume (passwd(5)).

EXAMPLES
    permit nopass :wheel cmd pkg
    deny anna as root

SEE ALSO
    doas(1), passwd(5), index(7)
